mastery.question_text:
$AC$ is a diameter of a circle with centre $O$ and radius $10$ cm.
$BD$ is a chord perpendicular to $AC$ at $M$, with $AM = 4$ cm.
Find $BD$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (-2,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2,0);
\coordinate (B) at (-1.2,1.6);
\coordinate (D) at (-1.2,-1.6);
\coordinate (M) at (-1.2,0);
\draw (A) -- (C);
\draw (O) circle (2);
\draw (B) -- (M);
\draw (M) -- (D);
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\node[below right] at (M) {$M$};
\node[above, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] at ($(A)!0.5!(M)$) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\coordinate (Ma) at ($(M)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (Mb) at ($(M)!0.3cm!(B)$);
\draw (Ma) -- ($(Ma)+(Mb)-(M)$) -- (Mb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
